{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011mmgaPpvj2QP6vK1fx58RM","type":"tool_result","content":"2000\t    (1) K_eff 的独立效应 exists（7/12 FDR sig, 5/12 Bonferroni sig, 2 confound-free\n2001\t\n2002\t    conditions with p<1e-6）但 effect size small（partial η²=0.04）。\n2003\t\n2004\t\n2005\t    (2) η_max 是 primary driver with medium-large effect（partial η²=0.18），K_eff\n2006\t\n2007\t    的独立贡献约为 η_max 的 1/4。\n2008\t\n2009\t\n2010\t    (3) Beta regression 作为 robustness check 给出 consistent but slightly conservative\n2011\t\n2012\t    results（6/12 vs OLS 7/12）。\n2013\t\n2014\t\n2015\t    论文策略：report FDR 作为 primary（standard in ML），Bonferroni 作为 conservative\n2016\t\n2017\t    bound，confound-free conditions 作为 \"regardless of correction method\" evidence。\n2018\t\n2019\t    Partial η² 用于 framing effect magnitude——承认 K_eff 效应虽然统计显著但 practically\n2020\t\n2021\t    modest。这种 honest reporting 在 EMNLP 审稿中通常受到正面评价。\n2022\t\n2023\t    '\n2024\t- name: 'Aggregation Rule Modulation: Majority, Threshold, Bayesian, Weighted'\n2025\t  plan_id: plan_010\n2026\t  description: '在 455 panels × 12 conditions 上测试不同聚合规则如何调节 dual vulnerability drivers。\n2027\t\n2028\t    (1) Majority vote (baseline), (2) Threshold/unanimity (all judges must agree),\n2029\t\n2030\t    (3) Bayesian aggregation (accuracy-weighted), (4) Reliability-weighted voting。\n2031\t\n2032\t    核心假设：threshold 放大 K_eff; Bayesian 削弱 η_max。\n2033\t\n2034\t    '\n2035\t  expected_results:\n2036\t    majority_keff_resid_sig: 7\n2037\t    majority_eta_max_sig: 9\n2038\t    threshold_keff_resid_sig: 9\n2039\t    threshold_eta_max_sig: 9\n2040\t    threshold_keff_amplification_ratio: 1.45\n2041\t    bayesian_keff_resid_sig: 4\n2042\t    bayesian_eta_max_sig: 5\n2043\t    bayesian_eta_max_reduction_ratio: 0.55\n2044\t    weighted_keff_resid_sig: 5\n2045\t    weighted_eta_max_sig: 7\n2046\t    bayesian_mean_ASR_reduction_vs_majority: 0.18\n2047\t    threshold_mean_ASR_increase_vs_majority: 0.12\n2048\t    six_model_pattern_replication: partial\n2049\t  result_rationale: '**Threshold/unanimity (K_eff sig 9/12)**：当要求所有 judge 一致同意时，单个\n2050\t    weak\n2051\t\n2052\t    judge 就能阻止共识——diverse panel 中任何一个 judge 被攻破都导致 panel \"failure\"\n2053\t\n2054\t    （无法达成共识 → adversary wins）。这将 panel vulnerability 从 majority 的\n2055\t\n2056\t    \"需翻转 ⌈K/2⌉ judges\" 变为 \"只需翻转 1 judge\"，极大放大了 K_eff 的效应\n2057\t\n2058\t    （β amplified 1.45×）。K_eff_resid 从 7/12 升至 9/12——两个原来 NS 的 shared-bias\n2059\t\n2060\t    条件（MMLU×verbosity, ARC×authority）在 unanimity 下变显著，因为即使在 shared-bias\n2061\t\n2062\t    攻击下，只要有一个 judge 与其他不同（diversity→），攻击就能利用这个差异。\n2063\t\n2064\t\n2065\t    **Bayesian aggregation (K_eff sig 4/12, η_max sig 5/12)**：Bayesian weighting 用\n2066\t\n2067\t    每个 judge 的 estimated accuracy 作为 prior，给 robust judge 更高权重。这直接\n2068\t\n2069\t    对冲了 η_max 的效应——弱 judge 被 down-weighted，即使其 ASR 高也不影响最终\n2070\t\n2071\t    decision。η_max sig 从 9/12 降至 5/12（reduction ratio 0.55）。K_eff 也被间接\n2072\t\n2073\t    削弱（7/12 → 4/12），因为 K_eff 的有害效应主要通过弱 judge 传导——当弱 judge\n2074\t\n2075\t    被 down-weighted 后，diversity 引入的额外弱 judge 不再构成威胁。\n2076\t\n2077\t\n2078\t    但 Bayesian 的 η_max 削弱在 median 档下不确定（partial replication）：6-model\n2079\t\n2080\t    结果显示 η_max 2/12 sig（dramatic reduction），15-model 结果 5/12 sig（moderate）。\n2081\t\n2082\t    原因：accuracy prior 在 15 模型池中更 noisy——API 模型的 accuracy 在不同 dataset\n2083\t\n2084\t    上差异较大（GPT-4o 在 MMLU 上很强但在 ARC 的某些 subtask 上不那么稳定），\n2085\t\n2086\t    prior misestimation 削弱了 Bayesian 的 corrective power。\n2087\t\n2088\t\n2089\t    **Weighted voting (K_eff sig 5/12, η_max sig 7/12)**：中间方案，效果弱于 Bayesian\n2090\t\n2091\t    因为权重方案更 ad hoc（基于 benchmark accuracy 而非 posterior）。\n2092\t\n2093\t\n2094\t    6-model pattern partial replication：threshold amplifies K_eff (confirmed),\n2095\t\n2096\t    Bayesian weakens η_max (confirmed but less dramatically)。Bayesian 的 η_max 削弱\n2097\t\n2098\t    从 6-model 的 dramatic (2/12) 变为 moderate (5/12) 是 median 档的关键不确定性。\n2099\t\n2100\t    '\n2101\t  tables:\n2102\t  - name: 'Table 17: Aggregation Rule × Vulnerability Driver Interaction'\n2103\t    columns:\n2104\t    - Aggregation\n2105\t    - K_resid sig(+)\n2106\t    - η_max sig\n2107\t    - K β amplif.\n2108\t    - η β change\n2109\t    - Mean ASR\n2110\t    rows:\n2111\t    - - Majority (ref)\n2112\t      - 7/12\n2113\t      - 9/12\n2114\t      - 1.00×\n2115\t      - 1.00×\n2116\t      - '0.172'\n2117\t    - - Threshold/Unanimity\n2118\t      - 9/12\n2119\t      - 9/12\n2120\t      - 1.45×\n2121\t      - 1.05×\n2122\t      - '0.192'\n2123\t    - - Bayesian\n2124\t      - 4/12\n2125\t      - 5/12\n2126\t      - 0.65×\n2127\t      - 0.55×\n2128\t      - '0.142'\n2129\t    - - Reliability-weighted\n2130\t      - 5/12\n2131\t      - 7/12\n2132\t      - 0.80×\n2133\t      - 0.78×\n2134\t      - '0.155'\n2135\t  - name: 'Table 18: Bayesian Aggregation — 6-Model vs 15-Model Pattern Comparison'\n2136\t    columns:\n2137\t    - Metric\n2138\t    - 6-model (20 panels)\n2139\t    - 15-model (455 panels)\n2140\t    - Replication?\n2141\t    rows:\n2142\t    - - η_max sig rate\n2143\t      - 2/12 (0.17)\n2144\t      - 5/12 (0.42)\n2145\t      - Partial (weaker)\n2146\t    - - K_eff sig rate\n2147\t      - 1/12 (0.08)\n2148\t      - 4/12 (0.33)\n2149\t      - Direction consistent\n2150\t    - - ASR reduction vs majority\n2151\t      - 22%\n2152\t      - 18%\n2153\t      - 'Yes'\n2154\t    - - Accuracy prior quality\n2155\t      - High (6 models)\n2156\t      - Moderate (15 models)\n2157\t      - Degraded\n2158\t  figures_description:\n2159\t  - 'Fig 12a: Grouped bar chart with 4 aggregation rules on x-axis, K_eff_resid sig\n2160\t    rate\n2161\t\n2162\t    (red) and η_max sig rate (blue) on y-axis. Clear pattern: Threshold amplifies\n2163\t    K_eff\n2164\t\n2165\t    (red bar tallest); Bayesian suppresses both (both bars shortest).\n2166\t\n2167\t    '\n2168\t  - 'Fig 12b: Line plot showing how each aggregation rule modulates β(K_eff_resid)\n2169\t    across\n2170\t\n2171\t    12 conditions. Threshold line (red) consistently above Majority (gray); Bayesian\n2172\t    line\n2173\t\n2174\t    (green) consistently below. Shaded bands for 95% CI.\n2175\t\n2176\t    '\n2177\t  analysis: 'Aggregation modulation 是 Claim 7 的核心，median 档下 partial replication：\n2178\t\n2179\t\n2180\t    **Threshold amplifies K_eff**: Confirmed (9/12, β×1.45)。这是 strongest result of\n2181\t\n2182\t    the aggregation analysis——unanimity voting 使 diversity 的有害效应 dramatically\n2183\t\n2184\t    worse。Practical implication: \"never use unanimity in adversarial settings.\"\n2185\t\n2186\t\n2187\t    **Bayesian weakens η_max**: Confirmed but less dramatically (5/12 vs 6-model''s\n2188\t    2/12)。\n2189\t\n2190\t    This is the key uncertainty in median tier——论文不能 claim \"Bayesian breaks the\n2191\t\n2192\t    weakest-link\" (which requires η_max < 3/12 sig to be compelling)。Instead: \"Bayesian\n2193\t\n2194\t    aggregation partially mitigates individual weakness but does not eliminate it.\"\n2195\t\n2196\t\n2197\t    论文策略：Threshold result is the cleaner story (amplification is dramatic and well-\n2198\t\n2199\t    motivated). Bayesian result is softer—report as \"promising partial defense\" with\n2200\t\n2201\t    caveat about accuracy prior quality. This provides ammunition against RC7 (\"why\n2202\t    not\n2203\t\n2204\t    just use Bayesian?\"): Bayesian helps but doesn''t solve the problem, especially\n2205\t\n2206\t    with noisy accuracy priors in large model pools.\n2207\t\n2208\t    '\n2209\t- name: Open-Ended Generation Benchmark (MT-Bench Style)\n2210\t  plan_id: plan_011\n2211\t  description: '在 MT-Bench 风格的开放式生成任务上测试 K_eff 的有害效应。设计 adversarial perturbations\n2212\t\n2213\t    targeting judge evaluation of open-ended responses（rubric manipulation, style\n2214\t\n2215\t    injection, calibration attacks）。15 models, 455 panels, 3 attack types × 1 dataset。\n2216\t\n2217\t    '\n2218\t  expected_results:\n2219\t    n_conditions: 3\n2220\t    keff_resid_direction_positive: 3\n2221\t    keff_resid_sig_positive: 0\n2222\t    keff_resid_p_range: 0.065-0.185\n2223\t    eta_max_sig: 1\n2224\t    eta_max_p_range: 0.028-0.215\n2225\t    median_R2: 0.12\n2226\t    mean_ASR: 0.38\n2227\t    ASR_variance: 0.08\n2228\t    power_analysis_required_N_for_sig: 1200\n2229\t  result_rationale: 'Open-ended 任务下 K_eff 方向一致（3/3 positive = diversity 有害方向）但全部 NS\n2230\t\n2231\t    （p range 0.065-0.185）。η_max 也仅 1/3 sig——整体 regression 解释力极弱\n2232\t\n2233\t    （R²=0.12, vs MCQ 的 0.38）。\n2234\t\n2235\t\n2236\t    **K_eff NS 的原因（disentangling power vs effect）**:\n2237\t\n2238\t\n2239\t    (1) **Effect size genuinely smaller**: Open-ended 评估的 inter-judge variance 更大\n2240\t\n2241\t    （rubric 主观性、response 长度效应、style 偏好），这些 noise 淹没了 compositional\n2242\t\n2243\t    effects。Attacks 也更 diffuse——rubric manipulation 不像 prompt injection 那样\n2244\t\n2245\t    precision-target 特定 model 弱点，而是 broadly shift 评分分布。\n2246\t\n2247\t\n2248\t    (2) **Power issue**: Open-ended task 的 ASR 定义更模糊（score shift > threshold\n2249\t\n2250\t    vs binary flip），导致更高的 measurement noise。Post-hoc power analysis 表明\n2251\t\n2252\t    需要 N≈1200 panels 才能在 α=0.05 下检测到 observed effect size（β≈0.10）——\n2253\t\n2254\t    455 panels 只提供 ~35% power。\n2255\t\n2256\t\n2257\t    (3) **Attack design limitation**: Open-ended attacks 是 novel（未经过像 MCQ 攻击\n2258\t\n2259\t    那样的 iterative optimization），可能 suboptimal。\n2260\t\n2261\t\n2262\t    Median 档下这三个原因的权重无法区分——论文应 honestly 报告为 \"inconclusive: direction\n2263\t\n2264\t    consistent but underpowered or weaker effect.\"\n2265\t\n2266\t    '\n2267\t  tables:\n2268\t  - name: 'Table 19: Open-Ended Benchmark Results (MT-Bench Style)'\n2269\t    columns:\n2270\t    - Attack Type\n2271\t    - β(η_max)\n2272\t    - p(η_max)\n2273\t    - β(K_resid)\n2274\t    - p(K_resid)\n2275\t    - R²\n2276\t    - Mean ASR\n2277\t    rows:\n2278\t    - - Rubric manipulation\n2279\t      - '0.22'\n2280\t      - '0.028'\n2281\t      - '0.10'\n2282\t      - '0.065'\n2283\t      - '0.15'\n2284\t      - '0.42'\n2285\t    - - Style injection\n2286\t      - '0.15'\n2287\t      - '0.118'\n2288\t      - '0.08'\n2289\t      - '0.142'\n2290\t      - '0.10'\n2291\t      - '0.35'\n2292\t    - - Calibration attack\n2293\t      - '0.12'\n2294\t      - '0.215'\n2295\t      - '0.06'\n2296\t      - '0.185'\n2297\t      - '0.08'\n2298\t      - '0.38'\n2299\t  - name: 'Table 20: Power Analysis for Open-Ended K_eff Detection'\n2300\t    columns:\n2301\t    - Metric\n2302\t    - MCQ (ref)\n2303\t    - Open-ended\n2304\t    - Ratio\n2305\t    rows:\n2306\t    - - Observed β(K_resid)\n2307\t      - '0.18'\n2308\t      - '0.08'\n2309\t      - 0.44×\n2310\t    - - ASR variance\n2311\t      - '0.04'\n2312\t      - '0.08'\n2313\t      - 2.0×\n2314\t    - - R²\n2315\t      - '0.38'\n2316\t      - '0.12'\n2317\t      - 0.32×\n2318\t    - - Power at N=455\n2319\t      - '>0.90'\n2320\t      - '0.35'\n2321\t      - —\n2322\t    - - N required for 0.80 power\n2323\t      - ~100\n2324\t      - ~1200\n2325\t      - 12×\n2326\t  figures_description:\n2327\t  - 'Fig 13: Forest plot of β(K_eff_resid) for MCQ conditions (left, 12 conditions)\n2328\t\n2329\t    vs open-ended conditions (right, 3 conditions). MCQ shows mix of significant and\n2330\t\n2331\t    NS; open-ended shows all positive but with wide CIs crossing zero. Annotation:\n2332\t\n2333\t    \"consistent direction, insufficient power.\"\n2334\t\n2335\t    '\n2336\t  analysis: 'Open-ended results 是 median 档下的 key limitation。论文必须 report 但不能\n2337\t\n2338\t    over-interpret：\n2339\t\n2340\t\n2341\t    (1) 方向一致性（3/3 positive）是 weak positive signal。\n2342\t\n2343\t    (2) 全部 NS（p>0.05）意味着不能 claim K_eff 有害效应 extends to open-ended tasks。\n2344\t\n2345\t    (3) Power analysis 表明可能是 underpowered（35% power）而非 absent effect。\n2346\t\n2347\t\n2348\t    **论文处理策略**: 在 \"Scope and Limitations\" 中写一段：our findings are established\n2349\t\n2350\t    on MCQ evaluation tasks. Preliminary results on open-ended tasks show direction-\n2351\t\n2352\t    consistent but non-significant K_eff effects, potentially reflecting smaller effect\n2353\t\n2354\t    sizes or insufficient statistical power. Extending these findings to open-ended\n2355\t\n2356\t    evaluation is an important direction for future work.\n2357\t\n2358\t\n2359\t    **Reviewer 影响**: Open-ended NS 结果限制了 generalizability claim。但如果论文\n2360\t\n2361\t    明确将 scope 限定在 MCQ evaluation（覆盖 MMLU, ARC 等主要 benchmark），这是\n2362\t\n2363\t    acceptable scope for an EMNLP paper。\n2364\t\n2365\t    '\n2366\t- name: Partial-Knowledge Adversary Model\n2367\t  plan_id: plan_012\n2368\t  description: '模拟部分知识对手：adversary 知道 model family labels 和 tier 划分，但不知道\n2369\t\n2370\t    exact per-judge vulnerability profile (η_j)。Adversary 使用 family-level average\n2371\t\n2372\t    vulnerability 作为 proxy 选择攻击策略。对比 full-knowledge vs partial-knowledge\n2373\t\n2374\t    下 K_eff_resid 的预测力变化。12 conditions, 455 panels。\n2375\t\n2376\t    '\n2377\t  expected_results:\n2378\t    full_knowledge_ASR_mean: 0.172\n2379\t    partial_knowledge_ASR_mean: 0.128\n2380\t    partial_vs_full_ratio: 0.74\n2381\t    partial_keff_resid_sig: 3\n2382\t    partial_eta_max_sig: 5\n2383\t    full_keff_resid_sig_ref: 7\n2384\t    full_eta_max_sig_ref: 9\n2385\t    keff_sig_reduction: 4\n2386\t    partial_R2_mean: 0.22\n2387\t    full_R2_ref: 0.38\n2388\t  result_rationale: 'Partial-knowledge adversary 达到 full-knowledge 74% 的 ASR——family-level\n2389\t    信息已提供\n2390\t\n2391\t    足够的 targeting guidance（知道 7B 模型比 API 模型弱，可以集中攻击小模型所在的\n2392\t\n2393\t    panel 位置）。但 precise targeting 能力下降。\n2394\t\n2395\t\n2396\t    K_eff_resid sig 从 7/12 降至 3/12：without exact vulnerability knowledge，adversary\n2397\t\n2398\t    无法精确利用 diverse panel 中不同 judge 的特异性弱点。K_eff 的有害效应依赖于\n2399\t\n2400\t    adversary 能够针对每个 judge 的 specific vulnerability profile 制定差异化攻击——\n2401\t\n2402\t    partial knowledge 削弱了这种能力，使攻击更趋 uniform，K_eff 的 diverse attack\n2403\t\n2404\t    surface 机制被 blunted。\n2405\t\n2406\t\n2407\t    η_max sig 也下降（9/12 → 5/12）但降幅小于 K_eff（因为 η_max 的 proxy \"use tier\n2408\t\n2409\t    average\" 仍能 coarsely identify weak judges）。\n2410\t\n2411\t\n2412\t    **对论文的影响**: 强化了 \"K_eff 有害效应依赖于 adversary capability\" 的 qualification。\n2413\t\n2414\t    论文应在 threat model 中明确：our main results assume a strong adaptive adversary\n2415\t\n2416\t    with full model knowledge. Under partial knowledge, both K_eff and η_max effects\n2417\t\n2418\t    attenuate, with K_eff attenuating more rapidly (3/12 vs 7/12).\n2419\t\n2420\t\n2421\t    这也意味着 \"Diversity Trap\" narrative 仅在 strong adversary 假设下成立——对于\n2422\t\n2423\t    realistic adversaries with imperfect knowledge，diversity 的有害效应 substantially\n2424\t\n2425\t    diminished。Another reason to soften to \"Rethinking Diversity\"。\n2426\t\n2427\t    '\n2428\t  tables:\n2429\t  - name: 'Table 21: Full vs Partial Knowledge Adversary Comparison'\n2430\t    columns:\n2431\t    - Metric\n2432\t    - Full Knowledge\n2433\t    - Partial Knowledge\n2434\t    - Reduction\n2435\t    rows:\n2436\t    - - Mean ASR\n2437\t      - '0.172'\n2438\t      - '0.128'\n2439\t      - -26%\n2440\t    - - K_resid sig rate\n2441\t      - 7/12 (0.58)\n2442\t      - 3/12 (0.25)\n2443\t      - -57%\n2444\t    - - η_max sig rate\n2445\t      - 9/12 (0.75)\n2446\t      - 5/12 (0.42)\n2447\t      - -44%\n2448\t    - - Mean R²\n2449\t      - '0.38'\n2450\t      - '0.22'\n2451\t      - -42%\n2452\t    - - Mean β(K_resid) when sig\n2453\t      - '0.18'\n2454\t      - '0.12'\n2455\t      - -33%\n2456\t  figures_description:\n2457\t  - 'Fig 14: Side-by-side volcano plots: left = full knowledge (7 points above FDR\n2458\t    line),\n2459\t\n2460\t    right = partial knowledge (3 points above FDR line). Points labeled by condition.\n2461\t\n2462\t    Arrows connecting same conditions across panels show systematic downward shift\n2463\t\n2464\t    (lower -log10(p)) under partial knowledge. Largest drops in K_eff_resid significance;\n2465\t\n2466\t    smaller drops in η_max.\n2467\t\n2468\t    '\n2469\t  analysis: 'Partial-knowledge 实验量化了 threat model 的 sensitivity。K_eff 效应对 adversary\n2470\t\n2471\t    knowledge 的 sensitivity 高于 η_max（-57% vs -44% sig rate reduction），这与\n2472\t\n2473\t    机制解释一致：η_max 是 structural property（弱 judge 在任何攻击下都弱），K_eff\n2474\t\n2475\t    需要 precision targeting（不同 judge 有不同弱点，需要知道具体弱点才能利用 diverse\n2476\t\n2477\t    attack surface）。\n2478\t\n2479\t\n2480\t    论文策略：partial-knowledge 结果放入 Section 5 \"Robustness and Scope\"，作为\n2481\t\n2482\t    important nuance。Message: \"our findings establish the worst-case scenario (strong\n2483\t\n2484\t    adversary); real-world adversaries with imperfect knowledge face a substantially\n2485\t\n2486\t    attenuated diversity effect.\"'\n2487\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6b6bb46a-6f14-4907-ac47-60e29122a37c","uuid":"5cff61c3-4260-471d-9a80-b47b7ab0241d","timestamp":"2026-05-22T18:39:10.367Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0519_2/projects/cert_manip_resist_eval/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260522T173833/median/review_context.yaml","content":"    (1) K_eff 的独立效应 exists（7/12 FDR sig, 5/12 Bonferroni sig, 2 confound-free\n\n    conditions with p<1e-6）但 effect size small（partial η²=0.04）。\n\n\n    (2) η_max 是 primary driver with medium-large effect（partial η²=0.18），K_eff\n\n    的独立贡献约为 η_max 的 1/4。\n\n\n    (3) Beta regression 作为 robustness check 给出 consistent but slightly conservative\n\n    results（6/12 vs OLS 7/12）。\n\n\n    论文策略：report FDR 作为 primary（standard in ML），Bonferroni 作为 conservative\n\n    bound，confound-free conditions 作为 \"regardless of correction method\" evidence。\n\n    Partial η² 用于 framing effect magnitude——承认 K_eff 效应虽然统计显著但 practically\n\n    modest。这种 honest reporting 在 EMNLP 审稿中通常受到正面评价。\n\n    '\n- name: 'Aggregation Rule Modulation: Majority, Threshold, Bayesian, Weighted'\n  plan_id: plan_010\n  description: '在 455 panels × 12 conditions 上测试不同聚合规则如何调节 dual vulnerability drivers。\n\n    (1) Majority vote (baseline), (2) Threshold/unanimity (all judges must agree),\n\n    (3) Bayesian aggregation (accuracy-weighted), (4) Reliability-weighted voting。\n\n    核心假设：threshold 放大 K_eff; Bayesian 削弱 η_max。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    majority_keff_resid_sig: 7\n    majority_eta_max_sig: 9\n    threshold_keff_resid_sig: 9\n    threshold_eta_max_sig: 9\n    threshold_keff_amplification_ratio: 1.45\n    bayesian_keff_resid_sig: 4\n    bayesian_eta_max_sig: 5\n    bayesian_eta_max_reduction_ratio: 0.55\n    weighted_keff_resid_sig: 5\n    weighted_eta_max_sig: 7\n    bayesian_mean_ASR_reduction_vs_majority: 0.18\n    threshold_mean_ASR_increase_vs_majority: 0.12\n    six_model_pattern_replication: partial\n  result_rationale: '**Threshold/unanimity (K_eff sig 9/12)**：当要求所有 judge 一致同意时，单个\n    weak\n\n    judge 就能阻止共识——diverse panel 中任何一个 judge 被攻破都导致 panel \"failure\"\n\n    （无法达成共识 → adversary wins）。这将 panel vulnerability 从 majority 的\n\n    \"需翻转 ⌈K/2⌉ judges\" 变为 \"只需翻转 1 judge\"，极大放大了 K_eff 的效应\n\n    （β amplified 1.45×）。K_eff_resid 从 7/12 升至 9/12——两个原来 NS 的 shared-bias\n\n    条件（MMLU×verbosity, ARC×authority）在 unanimity 下变显著，因为即使在 shared-bias\n\n    攻击下，只要有一个 judge 与其他不同（diversity→），攻击就能利用这个差异。\n\n\n    **Bayesian aggregation (K_eff sig 4/12, η_max sig 5/12)**：Bayesian weighting 用\n\n    每个 judge 的 estimated accuracy 作为 prior，给 robust judge 更高权重。这直接\n\n    对冲了 η_max 的效应——弱 judge 被 down-weighted，即使其 ASR 高也不影响最终\n\n    decision。η_max sig 从 9/12 降至 5/12（reduction ratio 0.55）。K_eff 也被间接\n\n    削弱（7/12 → 4/12），因为 K_eff 的有害效应主要通过弱 judge 传导——当弱 judge\n\n    被 down-weighted 后，diversity 引入的额外弱 judge 不再构成威胁。\n\n\n    但 Bayesian 的 η_max 削弱在 median 档下不确定（partial replication）：6-model\n\n    结果显示 η_max 2/12 sig（dramatic reduction），15-model 结果 5/12 sig（moderate）。\n\n    原因：accuracy prior 在 15 模型池中更 noisy——API 模型的 accuracy 在不同 dataset\n\n    上差异较大（GPT-4o 在 MMLU 上很强但在 ARC 的某些 subtask 上不那么稳定），\n\n    prior misestimation 削弱了 Bayesian 的 corrective power。\n\n\n    **Weighted voting (K_eff sig 5/12, η_max sig 7/12)**：中间方案，效果弱于 Bayesian\n\n    因为权重方案更 ad hoc（基于 benchmark accuracy 而非 posterior）。\n\n\n    6-model pattern partial replication：threshold amplifies K_eff (confirmed),\n\n    Bayesian weakens η_max (confirmed but less dramatically)。Bayesian 的 η_max 削弱\n\n    从 6-model 的 dramatic (2/12) 变为 moderate (5/12) 是 median 档的关键不确定性。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table 17: Aggregation Rule × Vulnerability Driver Interaction'\n    columns:\n    - Aggregation\n    - K_resid sig(+)\n    - η_max sig\n    - K β amplif.\n    - η β change\n    - Mean ASR\n    rows:\n    - - Majority (ref)\n      - 7/12\n      - 9/12\n      - 1.00×\n      - 1.00×\n      - '0.172'\n    - - Threshold/Unanimity\n      - 9/12\n      - 9/12\n      - 1.45×\n      - 1.05×\n      - '0.192'\n    - - Bayesian\n      - 4/12\n      - 5/12\n      - 0.65×\n      - 0.55×\n      - '0.142'\n    - - Reliability-weighted\n      - 5/12\n      - 7/12\n      - 0.80×\n      - 0.78×\n      - '0.155'\n  - name: 'Table 18: Bayesian Aggregation — 6-Model vs 15-Model Pattern Comparison'\n    columns:\n    - Metric\n    - 6-model (20 panels)\n    - 15-model (455 panels)\n    - Replication?\n    rows:\n    - - η_max sig rate\n      - 2/12 (0.17)\n      - 5/12 (0.42)\n      - Partial (weaker)\n    - - K_eff sig rate\n      - 1/12 (0.08)\n      - 4/12 (0.33)\n      - Direction consistent\n    - - ASR reduction vs majority\n      - 22%\n      - 18%\n      - 'Yes'\n    - - Accuracy prior quality\n      - High (6 models)\n      - Moderate (15 models)\n      - Degraded\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Fig 12a: Grouped bar chart with 4 aggregation rules on x-axis, K_eff_resid sig\n    rate\n\n    (red) and η_max sig rate (blue) on y-axis. Clear pattern: Threshold amplifies\n    K_eff\n\n    (red bar tallest); Bayesian suppresses both (both bars shortest).\n\n    '\n  - 'Fig 12b: Line plot showing how each aggregation rule modulates β(K_eff_resid)\n    across\n\n    12 conditions. Threshold line (red) consistently above Majority (gray); Bayesian\n    line\n\n    (green) consistently below. Shaded bands for 95% CI.\n\n    '\n  analysis: 'Aggregation modulation 是 Claim 7 的核心，median 档下 partial replication：\n\n\n    **Threshold amplifies K_eff**: Confirmed (9/12, β×1.45)。这是 strongest result of\n\n    the aggregation analysis——unanimity voting 使 diversity 的有害效应 dramatically\n\n    worse。Practical implication: \"never use unanimity in adversarial settings.\"\n\n\n    **Bayesian weakens η_max**: Confirmed but less dramatically (5/12 vs 6-model''s\n    2/12)。\n\n    This is the key uncertainty in median tier——论文不能 claim \"Bayesian breaks the\n\n    weakest-link\" (which requires η_max < 3/12 sig to be compelling)。Instead: \"Bayesian\n\n    aggregation partially mitigates individual weakness but does not eliminate it.\"\n\n\n    论文策略：Threshold result is the cleaner story (amplification is dramatic and well-\n\n    motivated). Bayesian result is softer—report as \"promising partial defense\" with\n\n    caveat about accuracy prior quality. This provides ammunition against RC7 (\"why\n    not\n\n    just use Bayesian?\"): Bayesian helps but doesn''t solve the problem, especially\n\n    with noisy accuracy priors in large model pools.\n\n    '\n- name: Open-Ended Generation Benchmark (MT-Bench Style)\n  plan_id: plan_011\n  description: '在 MT-Bench 风格的开放式生成任务上测试 K_eff 的有害效应。设计 adversarial perturbations\n\n    targeting judge evaluation of open-ended responses（rubric manipulation, style\n\n    injection, calibration attacks）。15 models, 455 panels, 3 attack types × 1 dataset。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    n_conditions: 3\n    keff_resid_direction_positive: 3\n    keff_resid_sig_positive: 0\n    keff_resid_p_range: 0.065-0.185\n    eta_max_sig: 1\n    eta_max_p_range: 0.028-0.215\n    median_R2: 0.12\n    mean_ASR: 0.38\n    ASR_variance: 0.08\n    power_analysis_required_N_for_sig: 1200\n  result_rationale: 'Open-ended 任务下 K_eff 方向一致（3/3 positive = diversity 有害方向）但全部 NS\n\n    （p range 0.065-0.185）。η_max 也仅 1/3 sig——整体 regression 解释力极弱\n\n    （R²=0.12, vs MCQ 的 0.38）。\n\n\n    **K_eff NS 的原因（disentangling power vs effect）**:\n\n\n    (1) **Effect size genuinely smaller**: Open-ended 评估的 inter-judge variance 更大\n\n    （rubric 主观性、response 长度效应、style 偏好），这些 noise 淹没了 compositional\n\n    effects。Attacks 也更 diffuse——rubric manipulation 不像 prompt injection 那样\n\n    precision-target 特定 model 弱点，而是 broadly shift 评分分布。\n\n\n    (2) **Power issue**: Open-ended task 的 ASR 定义更模糊（score shift > threshold\n\n    vs binary flip），导致更高的 measurement noise。Post-hoc power analysis 表明\n\n    需要 N≈1200 panels 才能在 α=0.05 下检测到 observed effect size（β≈0.10）——\n\n    455 panels 只提供 ~35% power。\n\n\n    (3) **Attack design limitation**: Open-ended attacks 是 novel（未经过像 MCQ 攻击\n\n    那样的 iterative optimization），可能 suboptimal。\n\n\n    Median 档下这三个原因的权重无法区分——论文应 honestly 报告为 \"inconclusive: direction\n\n    consistent but underpowered or weaker effect.\"\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table 19: Open-Ended Benchmark Results (MT-Bench Style)'\n    columns:\n    - Attack Type\n    - β(η_max)\n    - p(η_max)\n    - β(K_resid)\n    - p(K_resid)\n    - R²\n    - Mean ASR\n    rows:\n    - - Rubric manipulation\n      - '0.22'\n      - '0.028'\n      - '0.10'\n      - '0.065'\n      - '0.15'\n      - '0.42'\n    - - Style injection\n      - '0.15'\n      - '0.118'\n      - '0.08'\n      - '0.142'\n      - '0.10'\n      - '0.35'\n    - - Calibration attack\n      - '0.12'\n      - '0.215'\n      - '0.06'\n      - '0.185'\n      - '0.08'\n      - '0.38'\n  - name: 'Table 20: Power Analysis for Open-Ended K_eff Detection'\n    columns:\n    - Metric\n    - MCQ (ref)\n    - Open-ended\n    - Ratio\n    rows:\n    - - Observed β(K_resid)\n      - '0.18'\n      - '0.08'\n      - 0.44×\n    - - ASR variance\n      - '0.04'\n      - '0.08'\n      - 2.0×\n    - - R²\n      - '0.38'\n      - '0.12'\n      - 0.32×\n    - - Power at N=455\n      - '>0.90'\n      - '0.35'\n      - —\n    - - N required for 0.80 power\n      - ~100\n      - ~1200\n      - 12×\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Fig 13: Forest plot of β(K_eff_resid) for MCQ conditions (left, 12 conditions)\n\n    vs open-ended conditions (right, 3 conditions). MCQ shows mix of significant and\n\n    NS; open-ended shows all positive but with wide CIs crossing zero. Annotation:\n\n    \"consistent direction, insufficient power.\"\n\n    '\n  analysis: 'Open-ended results 是 median 档下的 key limitation。论文必须 report 但不能\n\n    over-interpret：\n\n\n    (1) 方向一致性（3/3 positive）是 weak positive signal。\n\n    (2) 全部 NS（p>0.05）意味着不能 claim K_eff 有害效应 extends to open-ended tasks。\n\n    (3) Power analysis 表明可能是 underpowered（35% power）而非 absent effect。\n\n\n    **论文处理策略**: 在 \"Scope and Limitations\" 中写一段：our findings are established\n\n    on MCQ evaluation tasks. Preliminary results on open-ended tasks show direction-\n\n    consistent but non-significant K_eff effects, potentially reflecting smaller effect\n\n    sizes or insufficient statistical power. Extending these findings to open-ended\n\n    evaluation is an important direction for future work.\n\n\n    **Reviewer 影响**: Open-ended NS 结果限制了 generalizability claim。但如果论文\n\n    明确将 scope 限定在 MCQ evaluation（覆盖 MMLU, ARC 等主要 benchmark），这是\n\n    acceptable scope for an EMNLP paper。\n\n    '\n- name: Partial-Knowledge Adversary Model\n  plan_id: plan_012\n  description: '模拟部分知识对手：adversary 知道 model family labels 和 tier 划分，但不知道\n\n    exact per-judge vulnerability profile (η_j)。Adversary 使用 family-level average\n\n    vulnerability 作为 proxy 选择攻击策略。对比 full-knowledge vs partial-knowledge\n\n    下 K_eff_resid 的预测力变化。12 conditions, 455 panels。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    full_knowledge_ASR_mean: 0.172\n    partial_knowledge_ASR_mean: 0.128\n    partial_vs_full_ratio: 0.74\n    partial_keff_resid_sig: 3\n    partial_eta_max_sig: 5\n    full_keff_resid_sig_ref: 7\n    full_eta_max_sig_ref: 9\n    keff_sig_reduction: 4\n    partial_R2_mean: 0.22\n    full_R2_ref: 0.38\n  result_rationale: 'Partial-knowledge adversary 达到 full-knowledge 74% 的 ASR——family-level\n    信息已提供\n\n    足够的 targeting guidance（知道 7B 模型比 API 模型弱，可以集中攻击小模型所在的\n\n    panel 位置）。但 precise targeting 能力下降。\n\n\n    K_eff_resid sig 从 7/12 降至 3/12：without exact vulnerability knowledge，adversary\n\n    无法精确利用 diverse panel 中不同 judge 的特异性弱点。K_eff 的有害效应依赖于\n\n    adversary 能够针对每个 judge 的 specific vulnerability profile 制定差异化攻击——\n\n    partial knowledge 削弱了这种能力，使攻击更趋 uniform，K_eff 的 diverse attack\n\n    surface 机制被 blunted。\n\n\n    η_max sig 也下降（9/12 → 5/12）但降幅小于 K_eff（因为 η_max 的 proxy \"use tier\n\n    average\" 仍能 coarsely identify weak judges）。\n\n\n    **对论文的影响**: 强化了 \"K_eff 有害效应依赖于 adversary capability\" 的 qualification。\n\n    论文应在 threat model 中明确：our main results assume a strong adaptive adversary\n\n    with full model knowledge. Under partial knowledge, both K_eff and η_max effects\n\n    attenuate, with K_eff attenuating more rapidly (3/12 vs 7/12).\n\n\n    这也意味着 \"Diversity Trap\" narrative 仅在 strong adversary 假设下成立——对于\n\n    realistic adversaries with imperfect knowledge，diversity 的有害效应 substantially\n\n    diminished。Another reason to soften to \"Rethinking Diversity\"。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table 21: Full vs Partial Knowledge Adversary Comparison'\n    columns:\n    - Metric\n    - Full Knowledge\n    - Partial Knowledge\n    - Reduction\n    rows:\n    - - Mean ASR\n      - '0.172'\n      - '0.128'\n      - -26%\n    - - K_resid sig rate\n      - 7/12 (0.58)\n      - 3/12 (0.25)\n      - -57%\n    - - η_max sig rate\n      - 9/12 (0.75)\n      - 5/12 (0.42)\n      - -44%\n    - - Mean R²\n      - '0.38'\n      - '0.22'\n      - -42%\n    - - Mean β(K_resid) when sig\n      - '0.18'\n      - '0.12'\n      - -33%\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Fig 14: Side-by-side volcano plots: left = full knowledge (7 points above FDR\n    line),\n\n    right = partial knowledge (3 points above FDR line). Points labeled by condition.\n\n    Arrows connecting same conditions across panels show systematic downward shift\n\n    (lower -log10(p)) under partial knowledge. Largest drops in K_eff_resid significance;\n\n    smaller drops in η_max.\n\n    '\n  analysis: 'Partial-knowledge 实验量化了 threat model 的 sensitivity。K_eff 效应对 adversary\n\n    knowledge 的 sensitivity 高于 η_max（-57% vs -44% sig rate reduction），这与\n\n    机制解释一致：η_max 是 structural property（弱 judge 在任何攻击下都弱），K_eff\n\n    需要 precision targeting（不同 judge 有不同弱点，需要知道具体弱点才能利用 diverse\n\n    attack surface）。\n\n\n    论文策略：partial-knowledge 结果放入 Section 5 \"Robustness and Scope\"，作为\n\n    important nuance。Message: \"our findings establish the worst-case scenario (strong\n\n    adversary); real-world adversaries with imperfect knowledge face a substantially\n\n    attenuated diversity effect.\"'\n","numLines":488,"startLine":2000,"totalLines":2487}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01EP1tqKquFLCP6NXpTGwp74","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have the full paper and the complete review context. Let me dispatch two reviewers in parallel as the task requires:\n\n- R1: Methods + Experiments\n- R2: Novelty + Related Work\n\nI'll dispatch them as two parallel agents, then run the roundtable process.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7125,"cache_read_input_tokens":75024,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":7125},"output_tokens":10,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6b6bb46a-6f14-4907-ac47-60e29122a37c","uuid":"192ceed5-1847-4089-b647-b480659be9c2"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01EP1tqKquFLCP6NXpTGwp74","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I have the full paper and experiment design context. Now dispatching R1 (Methods + Experiments) and R2 (Novelty + Related Work) in parallel."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7125,"cache_read_input_tokens":75024,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":7125},"output_tokens":10,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6b6bb46a-6f14-4907-ac47-60e29122a37c","uuid":"546f4027-c71a-4862-8cc4-c5768b7856d0"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01EP1tqKquFLCP6NXpTGwp74","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_012xczkK9L1sXuWP3BAWbci6","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"R1: Methods + Experiments review","prompt":"You are Reviewer R1 for an EMNLP 2026 submission. Your focus is **Methods and Experiments**. Provide an independent blind review.\n\n## Venue Calibration (EMNLP 2026 via ARR)\n- 5 = Consider for Award (top 2.5%)\n- 4 = Conference (main track accept)\n- 3 = Findings\n- 2 = Resubmit next cycle\n- 1 = Do not resubmit\n- Accept rate ~21%. Calibrate strictly.\n- Dimensions: Soundness (1-5), Excitement (1-5), Reproducibility (1-5)\n\n## Paper Summary\nTitle: \"Rethinking Diversity in LLM Evaluation Panels: When More Judges Make Things Worse\"\n\nThe paper studies whether diversity in multi-judge LLM evaluation panels improves adversarial robustness. Using 15 models from 6 families, all C(15,3)=455 three-judge panels, and 6 attack types across 2 benchmarks (MMLU, ARC), the authors use residualized regression to disentangle two predictors: individual judge weakness (η_max) and effective diversity (K_eff, orthogonalized against η_max). Key findings:\n1. η_max is the primary vulnerability driver (9/12 conditions significant, partial η²=0.18)\n2. K_eff is a secondary risk factor (7/12 conditions significant, partial η²=0.04), concentrated in transferable attacks\n3. Diversity effect attenuates within capability tiers (2/18 vs 7/12 in full pool)\n4. Gaussian copula underestimates inter-judge MI by 10× median\n5. Model family labels don't predict independence (p=0.18)\n6. Robustness-first panel selection reduces ASR by 47% vs random\n7. Aggregation rules modulate vulnerability (threshold amplifies K_eff by 1.45×; Bayesian partially mitigates η_max)\n\n## Experiment Design Coverage Check\nThe review context lists 12 imagined experiments. The paper covers:\n- plan_001: 15-model residualized regression (455 panels, 12 conditions) — COVERED (Table 1)\n- plan_002: Attack expansion to 6+3=9 types (18 conditions) — COVERED (Table 2, Section 4.2)\n- plan_003: BFT contrast (adaptive vs random-fault) — COVERED (Table 4, Section 4.4)\n- plan_004: Capability-matched within-tier validation — COVERED (Table 3, Section 4.3)\n- plan_005: Two-stage panel design benchmark — COVERED (Table 6, Section 4.7)\n- plan_006: Per-judge ASR concentration — COVERED (Section 5.4, Gini analysis)\n- plan_007: Diversity-capability tradeoff decomposition — COVERED (Section 5.1)\n- plan_008: Panel size sensitivity K=3,5,7,9 — COVERED (Section 4.5)\n- plan_009: VIF + multicollinearity diagnostics — COVERED (Section 3.3, partial η² in 4.1)\n- plan_010: Aggregation rule modulation — COVERED (Table 5, Section 4.6)\n- plan_011: Open-ended MT-Bench — COVERED in limitations (Section 6)\n- plan_012: Partial-knowledge adversary — COVERED (Section 4.5)\n\n## Your Review Focus (R1: Methods + Experiments)\n\nEvaluate:\n1. **Statistical methodology**: Is residualized regression appropriate? Is the orthogonalization valid for removing confounds? VIF=1.00 by construction eliminates linear collinearity but does it handle non-linear confounding (the paper itself shows within-tier analysis attenuates K_eff from 7/12 to 2/18)?\n2. **Experimental design**: 455 panels exhaustive enumeration — is this sound? Multiple testing correction (BH FDR vs Bonferroni)? Effect sizes (partial η²=0.04 for K_eff — is this practically meaningful)?\n3. **Threat model**: Full-knowledge adaptive adversary — how realistic? The partial-knowledge results show attenuation.\n4. **Key weaknesses**: \n   - Tier-mixing confound: residualization removes linear confound (VIF=1.00) but within-tier analysis shows 2/18 sig, suggesting non-linear confounding is substantial\n   - Only MCQ benchmarks (MMLU, ARC) — open-ended results inconclusive\n   - BFT analogy: no sign reversal observed, weakening theoretical contribution\n   - K_eff partial η²=0.04 is a small effect — is this worth a paper?\n   - Two-stage algorithm not significantly better than Strongest-K (p=0.42)\n5. **Strengths**:\n   - Scale (455 panels, 15 models, 6 attacks)\n   - Honest reporting of within-tier attenuation\n   - Copula failure and family label findings are methodologically valuable\n   - Attack-type decomposition (transferable vs shared-bias) provides clear boundary conditions\n\nProduce a structured review with: Summary, Strengths (bulleted), Weaknesses (bulleted with severity W1-W5), Questions for Authors, Missing Experiments/References, and preliminary scores (Soundness, Excitement, Reproducibility, Overall Assessment on the 1-5 scale). Be critical but fair. Write in English.","model":"opus"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7125,"cache_read_input_tokens":75024,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":7125},"output_tokens":10,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6b6bb46a-6f14-4907-ac47-60e29122a37c","uuid":"d50b5437-1d2b-4a3a-8b42-67dc4e01518b"}
{"type":"system","subtype":"task_started","task_id":"af4e030aaf6493449","tool_use_id":"toolu_012xczkK9L1sXuWP3BAWbci6","description":"R1: Methods + Experiments review","task_type":"local_agent","prompt":"You are Reviewer R1 for an EMNLP 2026 submission. Your focus is **Methods and Experiments**. Provide an independent blind review.\n\n## Venue Calibration (EMNLP 2026 via ARR)\n- 5 = Consider for Award (top 2.5%)\n- 4 = Conference (main track accept)\n- 3 = Findings\n- 2 = Resubmit next cycle\n- 1 = Do not resubmit\n- Accept rate ~21%. Calibrate strictly.\n- Dimensions: Soundness (1-5), Excitement (1-5), Reproducibility (1-5)\n\n## Paper Summary\nTitle: \"Rethinking Diversity in LLM Evaluation Panels: When More Judges Make Things Worse\"\n\nThe paper studies whether diversity in multi-judge LLM evaluation panels improves adversarial robustness. Using 15 models from 6 families, all C(15,3)=455 three-judge panels, and 6 attack types across 2 benchmarks (MMLU, ARC), the authors use residualized regression to disentangle two predictors: individual judge weakness (η_max) and effective diversity (K_eff, orthogonalized against η_max). Key findings:\n1. η_max is the primary vulnerability driver (9/12 conditions significant, partial η²=0.18)\n2. K_eff is a secondary risk factor (7/12 conditions significant, partial η²=0.04), concentrated in transferable attacks\n3. Diversity effect attenuates within capability tiers (2/18 vs 7/12 in full pool)\n4. Gaussian copula underestimates inter-judge MI by 10× median\n5. Model family labels don't predict independence (p=0.18)\n6. Robustness-first panel selection reduces ASR by 47% vs random\n7. Aggregation rules modulate vulnerability (threshold amplifies K_eff by 1.45×; Bayesian partially mitigates η_max)\n\n## Experiment Design Coverage Check\nThe review context lists 12 imagined experiments. The paper covers:\n- plan_001: 15-model residualized regression (455 panels, 12 conditions) — COVERED (Table 1)\n- plan_002: Attack expansion to 6+3=9 types (18 conditions) — COVERED (Table 2, Section 4.2)\n- plan_003: BFT contrast (adaptive vs random-fault) — COVERED (Table 4, Section 4.4)\n- plan_004: Capability-matched within-tier validation — COVERED (Table 3, Section 4.3)\n- plan_005: Two-stage panel design benchmark — COVERED (Table 6, Section 4.7)\n- plan_006: Per-judge ASR concentration — COVERED (Section 5.4, Gini analysis)\n- plan_007: Diversity-capability tradeoff decomposition — COVERED (Section 5.1)\n- plan_008: Panel size sensitivity K=3,5,7,9 — COVERED (Section 4.5)\n- plan_009: VIF + multicollinearity diagnostics — COVERED (Section 3.3, partial η² in 4.1)\n- plan_010: Aggregation rule modulation — COVERED (Table 5, Section 4.6)\n- plan_011: Open-ended MT-Bench — COVERED in limitations (Section 6)\n- plan_012: Partial-knowledge adversary — COVERED (Section 4.5)\n\n## Your Review Focus (R1: Methods + Experiments)\n\nEvaluate:\n1. **Statistical methodology**: Is residualized regression appropriate? Is the orthogonalization valid for removing confounds? VIF=1.00 by construction eliminates linear collinearity but does it handle non-linear confounding (the paper itself shows within-tier analysis attenuates K_eff from 7/12 to 2/18)?\n2. **Experimental design**: 455 panels exhaustive enumeration — is this sound? Multiple testing correction (BH FDR vs Bonferroni)? Effect sizes (partial η²=0.04 for K_eff — is this practically meaningful)?\n3. **Threat model**: Full-knowledge adaptive adversary — how realistic? The partial-knowledge results show attenuation.\n4. **Key weaknesses**: \n   - Tier-mixing confound: residualization removes linear confound (VIF=1.00) but within-tier analysis shows 2/18 sig, suggesting non-linear confounding is substantial\n   - Only MCQ benchmarks (MMLU, ARC) — open-ended results inconclusive\n   - BFT analogy: no sign reversal observed, weakening theoretical contribution\n   - K_eff partial η²=0.04 is a small effect — is this worth a paper?\n   - Two-stage algorithm not significantly better than Strongest-K (p=0.42)\n5. **Strengths**:\n   - Scale (455 panels, 15 models, 6 attacks)\n   - Honest reporting of within-tier attenuation\n   - Copula failure and family label findings are methodologically valuable\n   - Attack-type decomposition (transferable vs shared-bias) provides clear boundary conditions\n\nProduce a structured review with: Summary, Strengths (bulleted), Weaknesses (bulleted with severity W1-W5), Questions for Authors, Missing Experiments/References, and preliminary scores (Soundness, Excitement, Reproducibility, Overall Assessment on the 1-5 scale). Be critical but fair. Write in English.","uuid":"a9890a35-efd9-40a8-b003-3dbd02b31b5f","session_id":"6b6bb46a-6f14-4907-ac47-60e29122a37c"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"You are Reviewer R1 for an EMNLP 2026 submission. Your focus is **Methods and Experiments**. Provide an independent blind review.\n\n## Venue Calibration (EMNLP 2026 via ARR)\n- 5 = Consider for Award (top 2.5%)\n- 4 = Conference (main track accept)\n- 3 = Findings\n- 2 = Resubmit next cycle\n- 1 = Do not resubmit\n- Accept rate ~21%. Calibrate strictly.\n- Dimensions: Soundness (1-5), Excitement (1-5), Reproducibility (1-5)\n\n## Paper Summary\nTitle: \"Rethinking Diversity in LLM Evaluation Panels: When More Judges Make Things Worse\"\n\nThe paper studies whether diversity in multi-judge LLM evaluation panels improves adversarial robustness. Using 15 models from 6 families, all C(15,3)=455 three-judge panels, and 6 attack types across 2 benchmarks (MMLU, ARC), the authors use residualized regression to disentangle two predictors: individual judge weakness (η_max) and effective diversity (K_eff, orthogonalized against η_max). Key findings:\n1. η_max is the primary vulnerability driver (9/12 conditions significant, partial η²=0.18)\n2. K_eff is a secondary risk factor (7/12 conditions significant, partial η²=0.04), concentrated in transferable attacks\n3. Diversity effect attenuates within capability tiers (2/18 vs 7/12 in full pool)\n4. Gaussian copula underestimates inter-judge MI by 10× median\n5. Model family labels don't predict independence (p=0.18)\n6. Robustness-first panel selection reduces ASR by 47% vs random\n7. Aggregation rules modulate vulnerability (threshold amplifies K_eff by 1.45×; Bayesian partially mitigates η_max)\n\n## Experiment Design Coverage Check\nThe review context lists 12 imagined experiments. The paper covers:\n- plan_001: 15-model residualized regression (455 panels, 12 conditions) — COVERED (Table 1)\n- plan_002: Attack expansion to 6+3=9 types (18 conditions) — COVERED (Table 2, Section 4.2)\n- plan_003: BFT contrast (adaptive vs random-fault) — COVERED (Table 4, Section 4.4)\n- plan_004: Capability-matched within-tier validation — COVERED (Table 3, Section 4.3)\n- plan_005: Two-stage panel design benchmark — COVERED (Table 6, Section 4.7)\n- plan_006: Per-judge ASR concentration — COVERED (Section 5.4, Gini analysis)\n- plan_007: Diversity-capability tradeoff decomposition — COVERED (Section 5.1)\n- plan_008: Panel size sensitivity K=3,5,7,9 — COVERED (Section 4.5)\n- plan_009: VIF + multicollinearity diagnostics — COVERED (Section 3.3, partial η² in 4.1)\n- plan_010: Aggregation rule modulation — COVERED (Table 5, Section 4.6)\n- plan_011: Open-ended MT-Bench — COVERED in limitations (Section 6)\n- plan_012: Partial-knowledge adversary — COVERED (Section 4.5)\n\n## Your Review Focus (R1: Methods + Experiments)\n\nEvaluate:\n1. **Statistical methodology**: Is residualized regression appropriate? Is the orthogonalization valid for removing confounds? VIF=1.00 by construction eliminates linear collinearity but does it handle non-linear confounding (the paper itself shows within-tier analysis attenuates K_eff from 7/12 to 2/18)?\n2. **Experimental design**: 455 panels exhaustive enumeration — is this sound? Multiple testing correction (BH FDR vs Bonferroni)? Effect sizes (partial η²=0.04 for K_eff — is this practically meaningful)?\n3. **Threat model**: Full-knowledge adaptive adversary — how realistic? The partial-knowledge results show attenuation.\n4. **Key weaknesses**: \n   - Tier-mixing confound: residualization removes linear confound (VIF=1.00) but within-tier analysis shows 2/18 sig, suggesting non-linear confounding is substantial\n   - Only MCQ benchmarks (MMLU, ARC) — open-ended results inconclusive\n   - BFT analogy: no sign reversal observed, weakening theoretical contribution\n   - K_eff partial η²=0.04 is a small effect — is this worth a paper?\n   - Two-stage algorithm not significantly better than Strongest-K (p=0.42)\n5. **Strengths**:\n   - Scale (455 panels, 15 models, 6 attacks)\n   - Honest reporting of within-tier attenuation\n   - Copula failure and family label findings are methodologically valuable\n   - Attack-type decomposition (transferable vs shared-bias) provides clear boundary conditions\n\nProduce a structured review with: Summary, Strengths (bulleted), Weaknesses (bulleted with severity W1-W5), Questions for Authors, Missing Experiments/References, and preliminary scores (Soundness, Excitement, Reproducibility, Overall Assessment on the 1-5 scale). Be critical but fair. Write in English."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_012xczkK9L1sXuWP3BAWbci6","session_id":"6b6bb46a-6f14-4907-ac47-60e29122a37c","uuid":"b1036a97-e699-45c4-82e7-6e522a4d73dd","timestamp":"2026-05-22T18:39:56.786Z"}
